Title: The Open 2025: Rory McIlroy says Portrush win would be 'just as emotional' as Masters triumph
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"It would be amazing," the 36-year-old told BBC Sport NI when asked what a Portrush win would mean.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I think it would be just as emotional, if not more emotional than Augusta - and everyone saw the mess I was after that.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"It would be absolutely incredible. I\'m so grateful and appreciative of the support I get from home and they really make me feel that out there.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"That\'s an amazing feeling to play in front of and I want to embrace that this week. There\'s pressure internally to put on a show for everyone but I know that if I just go out and play my game, I\'m playing well enough to give myself a great chance."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 197}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I\'m so happy it\'s back so soon because I want to have another crack at it," he told BBC Sport.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 82}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I didn\'t have the week I wanted in 2019. I\'m a better player, manage my game better, and even if I have an off day, it\'s not going to be a 79 like it was on the first day in 2019."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': 'And this week he says he will not hide away from the attention.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 56}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I think I probably tried to isolate, and I think it\'s better for everyone if I embrace it," he added.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 90}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I think it\'s better for me because it\'s nice to be able to accept adulation, even though I struggle with it at times. But it\'s also nice for the person that is seeing you for the first time in a few years.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 163}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"It just makes for a better interaction."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 38}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I\'m certainly encouraged by how I\'ve played the last two starts, especially in Scotland," said 2014 Open champion McIlroy, who only managed four hours of sleep before his early practice round on Monday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 168}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"The two weeks off after the Travelers to reset, get over here, a bit of a change of scenery, has been really nice.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 19, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 96}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"When I was looking at the calendar for 2025, this was the tournament that was probably circled even more so than the Masters, for different reasons, so it\'s lovely to be coming in here already with a major and everything else that\'s happened this year.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 221}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I\'m excited with where my game\'s at, not that last week was a pure preparation but I definitely feel like it put me in a good spot heading into here."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 127}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Rory McIlroy says winning this week\'s Open Championship on home soil at Royal Portrush would be "just as emotional" as his career Grand Slam-clinching Masters victory.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 133}}], 'Image': []}
